# Copy this file to `.env` beside it and fill in what you need. `.env` is in
# .gitignore and must never be committed.
#
# Nothing here is required. A hub with no .env at all runs perfectly well: the
# admin panel still opens locked, and unlocking it is one button.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the hub

# The admin password for http://localhost:6059/ - the panel where the event
# key, the API keys and the mirror are set. Set it with:
#
#     python3 server/hub.py --set-admin-password
#
# which asks for it twice and writes the line below for you.
#
# The value is the password base64-encoded. THAT IS NOT ENCRYPTION: anybody who
# can read this file can decode it in one command. What it buys is that the
# password is not sitting in plain sight in a file that gets opened on a
# projector or read over a shoulder at a scoring table. Keeping the file off
# shared drives is what actually protects it.
#
# Leave it out entirely and no password is asked for.
#
#     ADMIN_PASSWORD_B64=cGFzc3dvcmQ=      # "password", as an example only

# ------------------------------------------------------------- the mirror

# Only on the machine running the off-site mirror - the hub does not read
# these. They are two different secrets on purpose: the push key is how the hub
# proves it is the hub (write), the view passcode is what a person types to
# read the site (read). See mirror/README.md.
#
# On a real host, prefer systemd's own Environment= lines over this file.
#
#     MIRROR_PUSH_KEY=the-long-generated-one
#     MIRROR_VIEW_PASSCODE=the-one-people-type
